\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces A trajectory in a generic MDP for AIG reduction, on AIGs of the Boolean function $f(x_1, x_2, x_3) = (\bar  {x_1}\land x_2,\ x_2 \land x_3)$. Every method surveyed in Section~\ref {sec:relwork} acts at this granularity: each action is one \texttt  {ABC} primitive applied to the whole graph, and the primitives of Section~\ref {sec:abc} preserve functional equivalence by construction, so every state reachable from $\mathcal  {G}_0$ still computes $f$.}}{3}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
